      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "Async onSave breaks the synchronous dispatch caller",
      "description": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it unawaited. The server in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise to res.end. Node's res.end throws a TypeError for a Promise chunk, so every POST /save request crashes the server. A writeFile rejection also goes unhandled, which crashes the process too. Make dispatch and the request handler await the result and catch errors. Then send the resolved string with res.end.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it unawaited. The server in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise to res.end.",
      "consequence": "Node's res.end throws a TypeError for a Promise chunk, so every POST /save request crashes the server. A writeFile rejection also goes unhandled, which crashes the process too.",
      "fix": "Make dispatch and the request handler await the result and catch errors. Then send the resolved string with res.end."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 8,
      "line_end": 8,
      "title": "New snapshot write has no covering test",
      "description": "The change adds a file write and an async return to onSave. The repository has no test that covers onSave. Regressions in the save path, like the broken caller, reach users without a failing test. Add a test that calls dispatch with save and checks the response text and the snapshot file contents.",
